    {
      "heading": "[508] config: hosts was REJECTED, now ACCEPTED",
      "answers": {
        "verdict_changes": true,
        "direction": "looser",
        "stored_value_changes": false,
        "already_signed_off": false,
        "real_clients": "no",
        "why": "Reproduced: config {hosts:['2459::52d2%lo0']} is rejected by the zod 3 oracle (hosts.0) and accepted by the merged build, so the verdict flips in the looser direction. Root cause is in src/schemas.ts: zod 3's z.string().ip() only accepted a %zone suffix on fe80:: link-local addresses (probe: fe80::1%eth0 -> [oracle true, now true]; 5ac3::de2a%wlan0 -> [oracle false, now true]), but the replacement zonedIpv6 refine accepts a zone on ANY string z.ipv6() can parse. review/corpus-diffs.md signed off the OPPOSITE direction (restoring fe80::1%eth0, which now produces no diff at all) and explicitly asserts the union 'reproduces exactly the set zod 3 matched ... so nothing *new* is let in' - the fuzzer shows that assertion is wrong, so this widening is not covered by the sign-off. stored_value_changes is false: these inputs were not accepted by both, and for the newly accepted ones the string is stored verbatim. real_clients 'no' is a judgement: a zone index is only meaningful for link-local addresses (and the one recorded caller used fe80::1%eth0), so I would not expect a well-behaved client to post 5ac3::de2a%wlan0. Judgement on impact: hosts are addresses the service will dial, so silently admitting malformed ones is an unreviewed loosening a human should either narrow (restrict the zone branch to fe80::/10) or sign off deliberately."
      },
      "claims": [
        {
          "claim": "A zoned non-link-local host is rejected by zod 3 and accepted by the merged build (verdict flip, looser).",
          "probe": "const c={hosts:['2459::52d2%lo0']};\nconst o=oracle.parseConfig(c), m=main.parseConfig(c);\nprint('oracle='+o.ok+' main='+m.ok);",
          "expect": "oracle=false main=true"
        },
        {
          "claim": "zod 3 only allowed a %zone on fe80:: addresses; the merged refine allows it on any IPv6. The signed-off fe80 address now shows no difference at all.",
